# VS Code REST Client. Run request 1 first -- every request below reads its token.
# REST Client only resolves {{name.response...}} within one file, which is why the
# login lives here rather than in auth.http.

@host = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. Log in as a client
# @name clientLogin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "zach",
  "password": "1234"
}

### Destinations, for the picker on the New Request screen
GET {{host}}/destination
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### My Trips. Scoped to the token -- there is no user id to swap.
GET {{host}}/request
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Trip detail. Carries the booking once a host has made one.
GET {{host}}/request/1
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### SECURITY: someone else's request. 403 -- request 4 belongs to dana.
GET {{host}}/request/4
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### A request that does not exist. 404, not 403.
GET {{host}}/request/999
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### SECURITY: a client reaching for a host route. 403 before it touches a controller.
GET {{host}}/host/request
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### SECURITY: registering while asking to be a HOST. Comes back CLIENT.
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sneaky@example.com",
  "username": "sneaky",
  "password": "1234",
  "role": "HOST"
}

### New request. 201.
POST {{host}}/request
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "destinationId": 3,
  "budgetPerPlayer": 1500.00,
  "playerCount": 4,
  "roundsRequested": 2,
  "nights": 3,
  "earliestStart": "2026-11-06",
  "latestStart": "2026-11-20",
  "notes": "Prefer a Thursday start"
}

### Invalid: no rounds, no players, budget of zero. 400, one message per problem.
POST {{host}}/request
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "destinationId": 3,
  "budgetPerPlayer": 0,
  "playerCount": 0,
  "roundsRequested": 0,
  "nights": 0
}

### A destination that does not exist. 400, not a foreign key crash.
POST {{host}}/request
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "destinationId": 999,
  "budgetPerPlayer": 1000.00,
  "playerCount": 2,
  "roundsRequested": 2,
  "nights": 2
}

### Invalid: half a window. 400 -- both ends or neither.
POST {{host}}/request
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "destinationId": 3,
  "budgetPerPlayer": 1500.00,
  "playerCount": 4,
  "roundsRequested": 2,
  "nights": 3,
  "earliestStart": "2026-11-06"
}

### Edit a request that is still pending (post-MVP). 204.
PUT {{host}}/request/2
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "destinationId": 2,
  "budgetPerPlayer": 2200.00,
  "playerCount": 2,
  "roundsRequested": 3,
  "nights": 3,
  "earliestStart": "2026-09-03",
  "latestStart": "2026-09-17",
  "notes": "Bumped the budget"
}

### Cancel a pending request. 204. The row survives as CANCELLED.
DELETE {{host}}/request/2
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Cancelling a booked trip. 400 -- too late.
DELETE {{host}}/request/1
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Accept the proposal. 204. It becomes the booking -- the only route to BOOKED there is.
POST {{host}}/request/51/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Turn the proposal down. 204. Back to PENDING, NOT declined -- the host can try again.
### Reason and note are both required; the note has a 10-character floor, because a
### refusal that says nothing sends the host back to the queue no better informed.
POST {{host}}/request/51/counter
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "DATES",
  "note": "That weekend is my nephew's wedding. Anything the week after works."
}

### The note floor. 400, with the message the counter sheet also shows while you type.
POST {{host}}/request/51/counter
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "PRICE",
  "note": "too much"
}

### SECURITY: accepting somebody else's proposal. 403 -- request 51 is not dana's.
POST {{host}}/request/4/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Explore: booked trips, anonymised (post-MVP)
GET {{host}}/explore
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Explore, filtered by cost per player and destination
GET {{host}}/explore?maxCostPerPlayer=1200&destinationId=1
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.$.token}}
